  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\nOption 1) 0.0016, 0.04, 0.2\n\n→ (0.2)² = 0.04\n\n→ (0.04)2 = 0.0016\n\nOption 2) (1)/({16)}, (1)/({4)}, (1)/({2)}\n\n→ ((1)/({2)})2 = (1)/({4)}\n\n→ ((1)/({4)})2 = (1)/({16)}\n\nOption 3) 2401, 49, 7\n\n→ (7)2 = 49\n\n→ (49)2 = 2401\n\nOption 4) 243, 81, 27\n\n→ (27)2 = **729** ≠ 81\n\n→ (81)2 = **6561** ≠ 243\n\nThus, out of all the options '243, 81, 27' is the odd one out.\n\nHence, \"Option 4\" is the correct answer.",
